          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Military Conquests</strong><br>\nNapoleon's military conquests reshaped the map of Europe. He expanded French territory and influence through a series of wars against various coalitions of European nations, often personally leading his troops into battle.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Continental System</strong><br>\nNapoleon attempted to weaken the British economy through the Continental System, which prohibited French and allied nations from trading with Britain. However, this strategy ultimately had mixed results and contributed to rising tensions in Europe.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Russian Campaign</strong><br>\nIn 1812, Napoleon launched an invasion of Russia, which ended in a disastrous retreat and significant losses for the French army. This failure marked a turning point in his military fortunes and led to a decline in his power.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
